{"canonicalText":"HomeOur ScienceFind a ProviderSystemAge™ TestFor ProvidersAboutResourcesSign In →Order Now →Introducing sex-specific results — trends and recommendations calibrated to your biologyView Sample ReportDismissFrequently Asked QuestionsGrounded in cutting-edge science and AI-powered technology, we help people identify risks before symptoms arise and implement clinically-relevant actions to slow and reverse aging.SearchSystemAge & ScienceOrdersSample Collection & ReturnSample & Report StatusTelehealth PolicyPrivacy & Terms01. SystemAge & Science02. Orders03. Sample Collection & Return04. Sample & Report Status05. Telehealth Policy06. Privacy & TermsSystemAge™ Test & The ScienceHow do we measure SystemAge™, and what science is it based on?The SystemAge™ section encompasses both overall SystemAge™ and functional SystemAge™ calculations for a total of 21 distinct systems. Each system represents a critical system contributing to the overall functionality of the body. SystemAge™ is calculated in the report by employing a \"noise barometer\" approach, which focuses on cytosines with stable methylation throughout life. Biological age is measured by quantifying the dysregulation of these cytosines, using the sums of standard deviations of their methylation values as biomarkers of aging and disease. This method identifies increased biological noise as a key indicator of aging and disease.Our science and approach is rooted in extensive research led by one of our co-founders Dr. Irina Conboy, a field expert with over 20+ years of experience, which strengthens our ability to advance in biological aging science and product development. For more detailed scientific information, please refer to the following publications:https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10522373/https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.10.09.617512What is BioNoise™?How's the overall SystemAge™ calculated compared to the SystemAge™ of 21 different systems?Is it normal to see a significant age difference between SystemAge™ and my chronological age?How do we calculate the SystemAge™ statuses (Optimal, Normal, Needs Attention) and what do they mean?What population are we comparing to?How do we measure the SystemAge™ (biological age) for different organs and systems using blood?Do we have details on the individual markers that went into each age report?What is the size of this reference population group?Why am I getting very different results from other biological age tests or clocks?Are 'Lifestyle Reflections' and 'Common Symptoms & Conditions' personalized?If all of my SystemAge™ numbers are younger or close to my chronological age, am I done?Will exercise affect the SystemAge™ of the Muscular System?Chronological Age vs. SystemAge™ (biological age)What do systems like Fibrosis and Oncogenesis indicate?How do you differentiate the female reproductive system from the male reproductive system?What are the major science updates of the SystemAge™ test?Why am I seeing significant changes between tests?How do females and males age differently in general?Experience the scienceDiscover your true biological age with our revolutionary testing technology.Test Your Biological Age Now →Generation LabSlow your aging with the world's most accurate epigenetic test and personalized insights. 460 biomarkers, 21 organs and systems.Order Now →Ask AI for a summary of the Generation LabHomeFind a ProviderSystemAge™ TestOur ScienceOur BiomarkersCareersAbout UsAuthorized PartnersFAQsFor ProvidersPublished ResearchGeneration Lab NewsLongevity Articles© 2025 Generation Lab, All rights reserved.info@generationlab.com+1 415 326 36561701 Old Bayshore Highway Burlingame, CA 94010Terms of ServicePrivacy PolicyTest ConsentResearch ConsentSlow Aging.Prevent Disease.Join our mailing listSubscribeWe'll only send the good stuff. You can unsubscribe anytime","document":{"attributes":{"lang":"en"},"children":[{"hidden":true,"tag":"head"},{"children":[{"hidden":true,"tag":"img"},{"hidden":true,"tag":"script"